 "notes": "ADMX-Orpheus dark photon search. 90% CL exclusion on kinetic mixing chi from Fig. 5 (top), extracted from the vector figure MixingAngleExclusion_v_mass_publication_downsampled.pdf in the arXiv e-print (lower envelope of the blue excluded fill region). Randomly polarized dark photon scenario, <cos^2 theta>=1/3, the paper's main result; polarized-scenario rescaling mentioned but not plotted. rho_DM = 0.45 GeV/cm^3 as labeled in Fig. 5, so no density rescaling applied. Mass from frequency via m = h f, covering 15.8-16.8 GHz (65.5-69.3 ueV). The full extracted curve (3687 points) was downsampled to 100 points by taking the median chi in equal mass bins; narrow upward spikes (up to ~5e-13 at tuning-step edges) and a narrow gap near 65.85-65.88 ueV where the limit exits the plotted range are smoothed over by the median.",
